----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* The recurring error "escaping closure captures non-escaping parameter 'content'" comes
  from a `glass(@ViewBuilder _ content: () -> some View)` helper that passes the
  non-escaping `content` into an escaping panel-builder closure. The same defect is present
  in ~16 AI* surfaces (e.g. *.Chrome.swift of AICrossRuleConflictDetection, AIFeatureCard,
  AIGeofenceAwareAutomationSuggestions, AIInboxAutoCategorization, AILifetimeStatsQA,
  AINLAlertBuilder, AINLAutomationBuilder, AINLDriveSearch, AINLSearch, AINLSqlPlayground,
  AIPiiRedactionSharedExports, AIQuietHoursSuggestion, AIRAGHelp, AISuggestNewGeofences,
  AIWatchFaceNLResponse, plus AISignalExplorerNlFilter / AIAutoNameUnnamedLocations).
  NOTE: VehiclePicker.Previews.swift uses the same helper SIGNATURE but in a non-escaping
  VStack builder, so it compiles cleanly (0 VehiclePicker errors on both platforms).
* These files are git-tracked at HEAD and were NOT modified by this prompt. `git status`
  shows only the 9 new VehiclePicker.* files added:
      ?? apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/VehiclePicker.Adapter.swift
      ?? .../VehiclePicker.AdapterTests.swift   ?? .../VehiclePicker.Model.swift
